WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.892 --> 00:00:17.958
Lady Anne was a good rider and managed to keep her seat as Lizzie took off down the

2
00:00:17.998 --> 00:00:22.060
road. But I could see that it wouldn't be easy for her to regain control.

3
00:00:23.061 --> 00:00:25.422
And an out-of-control horse is very dangerous.

4
00:00:26.482 --> 00:00:30.304
I let out several loud, shrill neighs, pawing the ground anxiously.

5
00:00:32.404 --> 00:00:35.446
A few seconds later, Blantyre came racing back down the path.

6
00:00:35.466 --> 00:00:37.847
"Oh no!"

7
00:00:38.307 --> 00:00:40.909
he exclaimed as he saw Lizzie galloping off with Anne.

8
00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.031
He flung the reins over my head and scrambled into the saddle.

9
00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.813
As soon as his feet were in the stirrups, I burst into a gallop.

10
00:00:50.214 --> 00:00:53.516
Blantyre gave me a free rein, seeing that I knew what to do.

11
00:00:54.757 --> 00:00:56.118
We raced after the runaways.

12
00:00:57.779 --> 00:00:59.860
For the first mile, we barely kept them in view.

13
00:01:00.948 --> 00:01:04.091
I was galloping as fast as I could, but Lizzie was even faster.

14
00:01:05.172 --> 00:01:07.674
Then the road curved to the right, and we lost sight of them.

15
00:01:10.296 --> 00:01:12.637
By the time we reached the curve, Lizzie had disappeared.

16
00:01:13.898 --> 00:01:17.261
The road split just ahead, and I wasn't sure which way to go.

17
00:01:18.302 --> 00:01:20.324
There was a woman standing at her garden gate.

18
00:01:20.544 --> 00:01:21.224
"To the right!"

19
00:01:21.685 --> 00:01:22.946
she called when she saw us.

20
00:01:22.966 --> 00:01:26.128
"Thanks!" Blantyre called back.

21
00:01:27.349 --> 00:01:28.170
We galloped on.

22
00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:30.652
For a while we barely caught sight of Lizzie.

23
00:01:31.932 --> 00:01:36.114
Luckily, after we'd lost them yet again, a road worker waved us down.

24
00:01:36.134 --> 00:01:38.576
"They turned that way, sir!"

25
00:01:38.936 --> 00:01:43.638
the worker called to Blantyre, pointing to an open area with lots of weeds and holes.

26
00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:47.661
It was the worst possible place for a gallop.

27
00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:51.823
When Lady Anne rode me there, we never went faster than a walk.

28
00:01:53.064 --> 00:01:54.845
We soon caught sight of Lizzie again.

29
00:01:56.345 --> 00:02:00.908
Lady Anne was still in the saddle, but she was swaying back and forth now, looking exhausted.

30
00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:05.789
I could see that she was pulling on the reins, but it wasn't doing any good.

31
00:02:06.889 --> 00:02:11.151
Lizzie was still going, though the roughness of the ground had forced her to slow from a gallop

32
00:02:11.191 --> 00:02:11.831
to a canter.

33
00:02:12.931 --> 00:02:14.551
That meant I had a chance to catch her.

34
00:02:15.312 --> 00:02:16.372
I surged forward.

35
00:02:18.072 --> 00:02:22.174
Blantyre had let me choose my own way while we were on the road, but now he took

36
00:02:22.254 --> 00:02:22.754
over again.

37
00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:27.955
With a light hand and a quick eye, he guided me expertly over the tricky ground.

38
00:02:29.276 --> 00:02:30.456
I barely had to slow down.

39
00:02:31.488 --> 00:02:32.828
We started to gain on Lizzie.

40
00:02:34.349 --> 00:02:37.090
About halfway across the open area was a wide ditch.

41
00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.891
I thought it might make Lizzie stop at last.

42
00:02:41.051 --> 00:02:45.732
Instead she leaped awkwardly across, stumbling on the rough ground on the far side.

43
00:02:47.773 --> 00:02:49.994
Lady Anne was flung to the ground and lay still.

44
00:02:51.914 --> 00:02:52.895
Blantyre groaned.

45
00:02:52.915 --> 00:02:56.236
"Now, Black Auster, do your best!"

46
00:02:56.676 --> 00:02:57.296
he urged me.

47
00:03:00.456 --> 00:03:03.218
I cleared the ditch with a strong leap, landing safely.

48
00:03:04.539 --> 00:03:06.861
Blantyre pulled me to a stop and leaped down.

49
00:03:08.001 --> 00:03:13.085
He ran to Lady Anne's side while I stood there, my sides heaving after the long gallop.

50
00:03:14.746 --> 00:03:16.647
Two men had been trimming weeds nearby.

51
00:03:18.128 --> 00:03:22.031
One was already chasing Lizzie, who had slowed down after losing her rider.

52
00:03:22.691 --> 00:03:23.972
The other ran toward us.

53
00:03:23.992 --> 00:03:25.754
"Oh no!"

54
00:03:26.234 --> 00:03:29.116
he said when he saw Lady Anne lying there still and pale.

55
00:03:30.124 --> 00:03:30.745
"How can I help?"

56
00:03:32.346 --> 00:03:33.107
"Can you ride?"

57
00:03:33.427 --> 00:03:34.408
Blantyre asked.

58
00:03:34.428 --> 00:03:37.350
"Not very well," the man said.

59
00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:39.833
"But I'll give it a try for Lady Anne's sake.

60
00:03:40.573 --> 00:03:42.735
She's always been so kind to my family."

61
00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:48.520
"Don't worry, this horse will take care of you," Blantyre said, gesturing to me.

62
00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:54.665
"Ride quickly to the doctor's house, then go to Earlshall and let them know what's happened."

63
00:03:56.207 --> 00:03:57.428
The man agreed and mounted.

64
00:03:58.624 --> 00:04:00.906
He wasn't a very good rider, but I didn't mind.

65
00:04:03.007 --> 00:04:06.249
We hurried to the doctor's house, and then back to Earlshall Park.

66
00:04:08.991 --> 00:04:14.435
A groom returned me to the stable while another quickly saddled Ginger for Lady Anne's brother and the

67
00:04:14.575 --> 00:04:15.856
others prepared the carriage.

68
00:04:17.917 --> 00:04:20.539
It seemed to take a long time before anyone returned.

69
00:04:21.599 --> 00:04:23.881
At last Ginger arrived back at the stable.

70
00:04:23.901 --> 00:04:28.304
"We galloped almost all the way there," she told me.

71
00:04:29.096 --> 00:04:30.938
"Lady Anne still wasn't moving.

72
00:04:32.219 --> 00:04:35.401
But the doctor was tending to her, and I heard him say she wasn't dead.

73
00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:40.346
Later I heard someone else say that she was lucky she hadn't broken any bones.

74
00:04:41.607 --> 00:04:43.028
So I expect she'll be all right."

75
00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:47.612
The next day Blantyre came to see me.

76
00:04:47.632 --> 00:04:53.176
"You're the finest horse I know, Black Auster," he said as he patted me fondly.

77
00:04:53.196 --> 00:04:57.320
"You seemed to understand the danger as well as I did.

78
00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.783
Thanks to your speed and heart, Anne will be fine in a week or two.

79
00:05:02.744 --> 00:05:07.188
And from now on, I'm sure she won't ever want to ride any other horse but you."
